# Copy this file to .env.local (untracked by git) and fill in your own
# Supabase project's values. Find these under Project Settings -> API in the
# Supabase dashboard.
#
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL is your project's REST/Auth endpoint, e.g.:
#   https://xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx.supabase.co
#
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY is the PUBLIC "anon" key. It is safe to ship inside
# the built frontend bundle (including a public GitHub Pages deployment)
# because every table is protected by Row Level Security — see
# /supabase/migrations/0003_rls_policies.sql. It is NOT a secret.
#
# NEVER put the "service_role" key in this file, in any VITE_ variable, or
# anywhere under src/. The service role key bypasses RLS entirely and must
# only ever be used server-side (e.g. exported as an env var on your own
# machine when running scripts/migrate_xlsm.py --commit).

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-public-key-here

# Optional. Overrides the Vite `base` path (see vite.config.ts). Leave unset
# for the default GitHub Pages project-site path (/shivansh-stores/). Set to
# "/" if you deploy to a custom domain or a user/org root site instead.
# VITE_BASE_PATH=/
